   "daf": "134a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "לֹא שָׁחַק מֵעֶרֶב שַׁבָּת. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: דְּבָרִים שֶׁאֵין עוֹשִׂין לַמִּילָה בְּשַׁבָּת — עוֹשִׂין לָהּ בְּיוֹם טוֹב. שׁוֹחֲקִין לָהּ כַּמּוֹן, וְטוֹרְפִין לָהּ יַיִן וָשֶׁמֶן.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «If one did not grind» the cumin «from Shabbat eve,» he chews it with his teeth and places it on the place of circumcision as a salve. «The Sages taught:» There are «actions that may not be performed» in preparation «for a circumcision on Shabbat» but «may be performed» in preparation «for it on a Festival.» For example: «One grinds cumin for it, and one mixes wine and oil for it.»"
  }
